.pnpm-debug.log*
# Acceptance evidence is a DELIVERABLE, not noise. `*.log` above is a runtime-output rule, but the
# transcript of the smoke run a phase CLOSES ON is the artifact itself, and its AC asserts the file
# is TRACKED (`git ls-files --error-unmatch`) — unsatisfiable while the blanket rule applies.
#
# This has already bitten silently once: .specs/codedm/phase10-smoke/real-smoke-run.log sits on
# disk believed committed, while `git ls-files` lists only the .ts beside it. It is NOT un-ignored
# here on purpose — that is another phase's evidence (and a FAIL verdict at that), so widening this
# to `!.specs/**/*.log` is that phase owner's call to make with their own artifact in hand, not a
# side effect of this one. Narrow by phase until then.
!.specs/codedm/phase0-smoke/*.log

